# One mark in the walk's state records that nothing was done in an iteration of a loop, or since an inlined copy began, and in which iterations no other code ran.
# Three kinds of edges rely on it. What comes before each of them either runs again or is not read again.
# Every entry of the effects tables may be right and the mark still false: at a join, or on a path where an operation is built and the state is not updated.
# With the run-time effects check, emitted code counts each operation that does something as it runs, by the traits that it was built with.
# Each of the edges crashes unless the count is what it was at the beginning. UnderstateEffects:RestartMark/all/RunsOtherCode makes the mark false on purpose.
# f1 = change, f2 = count, f3 = kernel, f4 = fill, f5 = atItsLength
# An iteration of the specialized version of a versioned loop restarts in the generic version, with the values of the loop header.
# The increment of `turns` comes before the call to change(), where the iteration exits.
# In a default build with the fault injected, the program prints 3011 17 and nothing else.
# RUN(TURN): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime mechanisms=all globalThis.pick = 0;
# TURN: 20 8
# TURN-NEXT: 3011 16
# TURN-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(TWICE): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:RestartMark/all/RunsOtherCode mechanisms=all globalThis.pick = 0;
# TWICE: 20 8
# TWICE: a loop iteration restarts in the generic version, so the compiler's state says that nothing observable happened in it, but an operation that is observable if repeated has run since it began
# TWICE-NOT: 3011
# TWICE: crashed
# TWICE: with
# An inlined copy whose speculation fails exits to the call that it replaces, and the callee runs from its start.
# The call to count() has already run when the inlined copy of the constructor finds that its class has another superclass.
# In a default build with the fault injected, the program prints 27 9 and nothing else.
# RUN(COPY): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime mechanisms=all globalThis.pick = 1;
# COPY: 27 6
# COPY-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(CALLED): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:RestartMark/all/RunsOtherCode mechanisms=all globalThis.pick = 1;
# CALLED: an inlined call falls back to the real call, so the compiler's state says that nothing observable happened in it, but an operation that is observable if repeated has run since it began
# CALLED-NOT: 27
# CALLED: crashed
# CALLED: with
# An iteration in which no other code ran is a quiet iteration. Its back edge skips the block before the loop header that reads for quiet iterations, where the length of the array was read.
# In a default build with the fault injected, the program prints 3 and nothing else.
# RUN(QUIET): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime mechanisms=all globalThis.pick = 2;
# QUIET: 9,0,1,2,3
# QUIET-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(LOUD): run-in-shell testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:RestartMark/all/RunsOtherCode mechanisms=all globalThis.pick = 2;
# LOUD: a loop iteration skips the loads that were hoisted for iterations without side effects, so the compiler's state says that no other code ran in it, but an operation that may run other code has run since it began
# LOUD-NOT: 0,1
# LOUD: crashed
# LOUD: with
# These operations are built only with the switch, and the sweep removes a BeginEffectsCheck that nothing refers to.
# RUN(WALK): walk f3:Body testing=CheckEffectsAtRunTime,UnderstateEffects:RestartMark/all/RunsOtherCode mechanisms=all
# WALK: = BeginEffectsCheck
# WALK: = PutModuleVariable
# WALK: = CheckIterationRestart
# RUN(BUILT): walk f3:Body mechanisms=all
# BUILT-NOT: BeginEffectsCheck
# BUILT-NOT: CheckIterationRestart
